# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STM32CubeIDE writes one directory per build configuration.
/Debug/
/Release/

# Object files, dependency files and the per-function stack/cyclomatic reports
# GCC emits alongside them.
*.o
*.d
*.su
*.cyclo

# Linked images and their listings. The .elf is what gets flashed; it is a build
# product, not a source.
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.srec
*.map
*.list
*.lst

# ── STM32CubeIDE / CubeMX scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# .mxproject is CubeMX's record of what it generated last time. It is derived
# from the .ioc and is rewritten on every generate.
.mxproject
MXTmpFiles/
*.ioc_bak

# Eclipse workspace leftovers. These appear when a project is opened, not when
# it is written, so they belong to whoever opened it.
.metadata/
RemoteSystemsTempFiles/
*.launch
*.bak
*~

# ── Editors and OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Deliberately NOT ignored - each of these is commonly excluded by copy-pasted
# STM32 gitignores, and every one of them would break a fresh clone here:
#
#   .project .cproject .settings/
#       These *are* the CubeIDE project. Without them a clone is a folder of C
#       files with no build configuration - no include paths, no -D defines, no
#       linker script, no toolchain. There is no .ioc to regenerate them from,
#       because this is a bare CMSIS project (see README).
#
#   Drivers/
#       Vendor CMSIS headers, but not optional and not fetched by any package
#       manager: without them nothing compiles. Trimmed to the five headers a
#       Cortex-M0+ GCC build actually reaches, so it costs ~676 KB rather than
#       the 3.4 MB the full CMSIS drop would.
#
#   Startup/startup_stm32c011f6ux.s, STM32C011F6UX_FLASH.ld
#       Part-specific and hand-placed. Nothing regenerates them.
#
#   Src/main.c
#       Ours, not generated. A CubeMX-flavoured gitignore would exclude it.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
